˜[ÉˆéÆƒÂ‡;éÚ√M°Ûª˘RÜßñ‘√S™`‰%ê{"url":"/gcsl/implementation/tooling-state/","fragment":{"page_number":0,"data":{"url":"/gcsl/implementation/tooling-state/","content":"300 Tooling State. GCSL tooling shares language analysis while keeping disk access and editor protocol handling outside the core. This prevents checking and formatting from depending on an evaluator run. 300.1 Source discovery # gcsl-disk finds workspace markers and returns a source collection with stable path and diagnostic mappings. It excludes hidden names and nested workspace trees when reading one workspace. The CLI and language server use this shared layer rather than implementing separate import rules. A check of a directory discovers workspaces. A format of a directory finds source files, including standalone files. Their traversal results are therefore intentionally different. 300.2 Editor snapshots # gcsl-lsp overlays open document text on disk sources and asks a worker to check the affected workspace. Queries use an up-to-date semantic index; they can force a pending check before answering. Diagnostics continue to refer to actual source even when a query temporarily repairs unmatched braces to find usable names. Rename computes proposed edits and checks their effect before offering them. Standard-library, file, and directory identities are not editable through that operation. Formatting returns edits from the language's formatter rather than applying the editor's formatting preferences. Only local file: document URIs with an empty or localhost authority and an absolute decoded path map to disk files. Other URI forms are checked as standalone documents, not treated as local workspace paths. 300.3 Formatter # The formatter works from tokens, comments, and parsed structure. It does not need evaluation or successful type inference. Syntax errors prevent a rewrite of that file. The CLI uses a temporary file and replacement so readers don't observe a partially written formatted file. The principal code is in crates/gcsl-disk/src/lib.rs, crates/gcsl-lsp/src/, crates/gcsl/src/index/, and crates/gcsl/src/fmt.rs. The CLI adapters live in crates/gcsl-cli/src/.","word_count":287,"filters":{},"meta":{"crumbs":"GCSL / gcsl-internals","title":"300 Tooling State"},"anchors":[{"element":"h2","id":"source-discovery","text":"300.1 Source discovery #","location":30},{"element":"h2","id":"editor-snapshots","text":"300.2 Editor snapshots #","location":101},{"element":"h2","id":"formatter","text":"300.3 Formatter #","location":225}]}},"word_data":{"live":[{"position":284,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"oper":[{"position":176,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"appli":[{"position":186,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"befor":[{"position":134,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":163,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"as":[{"position":216,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":221,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"intent":[{"position":99,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"author":[{"position":201,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"reader":[{"position":263,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"outsid":[{"position":16,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"usabl":[{"position":153,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"overlay":[{"position":106,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"even":[{"position":143,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"effect":[{"position":162,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"keep":[{"position":9,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"a":[{"position":40,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":76,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":79,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":83,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":86,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":115,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":131,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":145,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":249,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":257,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":266,"w